\[\frac{4}{(1 - 2b)^2} - \frac{1}{b^2} = 0 \implies \frac{4}{(1 - 2b)^2} = \frac{1}{b^2} \implies 4b^2 = (1 - 2b)^2 \implies 4b^2 = 1 - 4b + 4b^2 \implies 0 = 1 - 4b \implies 4b = 1 \implies b = \frac{1}{4}.\]
